From: Togo Tagai <mail@mikan.observer>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: bcma-hcd: honor DT shutdown delay

The Buffalo WXR-1900DHP3 OEM xHCI stop path applies a warm reset and then
waits five seconds.  Live testing also showed that removing the xHCI child
and waiting before reboot greatly reduces warm-reboot failures with a USB
3.0 storage device attached.

Honor an optional delay after OF children have been depopulated and before
the parent BCMA core is disabled.  The property keeps this board-specific
timing policy in DT instead of matching a machine compatible in the generic
host driver.  Reject excessive values to keep shutdown time bounded.

Signed-off-by: Togo Tagai <mail@mikan.observer>
---
 drivers/usb/host/bcma-hcd.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/usb/host/bcma-hcd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/bcma-hcd.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/syscon.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
@@ -540,9 +541,27 @@ static void bcma_hcd_remove(struct bcma_
 	bcma_core_disable(dev, 0);
 }
 
+static void bcma_hcd_shutdown_delay(struct bcma_device *dev)
+{
+	u32 delay_ms;
+
+	if (device_property_read_u32(&dev->dev, "brcm,shutdown-delay-ms",
+				     &delay_ms))
+		return;
+
+	if (delay_ms > 10000) {
+		dev_warn(&dev->dev, "ignoring excessive shutdown delay\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	if (delay_ms)
+		msleep(delay_ms);
+}
+
 static void bcma_hcd_shutdown(struct bcma_device *dev)
 {
 	bcma_hcd_of_platform_depopulate(bcma_get_drvdata(dev));
+	bcma_hcd_shutdown_delay(dev);
 
 	bcma_hci_platform_power_gpio(dev, false);
 	bcma_core_disable(dev, 0);
